{
  "_README": "Every option name `ffmpeg -h filter=<name>` declares for each filter in muvid.footage.edl.LOOK_FILTERS -- the filter's own AVOptions AND its child classes (scale carries SWScaler and framesync, whose options really are settable from a filtergraph string: `scale=w=64:h=48:dstw=800` is rc=0, and none of them moves the frame). This is a CENSUS, not the guard. The guard is muvid.footage.edl._LOOK_GEOMETRY_FILTERS, an ALLOWLIST of the options a look may set on the four filters that can change the output frame -- so an option absent from it is already refused at runtime. The census exists so that a new ffmpeg option becomes a DECISION someone records rather than a surprise refusal in production, and so that a typo in the allowlist is dead code a test can see. It is deliberately NOT trusted as complete: ffmpeg 6.1.6's `-h filter=scale` omits `s`/`size` while `scale=s=320x240` produces a 320x240 frame there (measured) -- which is exactly why the guard is an allowlist and not a classification of this file. Refresh with: python -c \"import tests.test_edl_look_options as t; t._refresh_snapshot()\" -- once per binary you want represented; the union accumulates. Never hand-edit it.",
